+// pins H3, H9, H16 (PLAN.md TAB-25, CMD-24): Cmd-W, a row's close button and
+// a middle click follow one rule. In a window with Spaces the close button on
+// an awake Space pin sleeps it, as Cmd-W does; once the pin is asleep, or
+// with Cmd-W's setting off, it closes. Outside such a window -- a web app's
+// window, a private window -- a pinned tab is Chromium's, and Cmd-W and a
+// middle click close it. The close button closed a Space pin for good, Cmd-W
+// slept a web app's pinned home tab, and in a private window Cmd-W and a
+// middle click on a pinned tab did nothing.
+IN_PROC_BROWSER_TEST_F(SidebarClickTest, OneRuleClosesOrSleepsAPin) {
